# XSH feof()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.feof.001
anchor     functions/feof.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/feof.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       On a stream reading "ab", feof() is 0 when it is opened, non-zero
           once fgetc() has returned 'a', 'b' and then EOF, and 0 again after
           clearerr(); on a stream whose error indicator alone is set (a
           read on its closed descriptor, then restored with dup2()), feof()
           is 0.
test       t/001-indicator.c

assertion  XSH.feof.002
anchor     functions/feof.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       With errno set to ERANGE, feof() on a stream whose end-of-file
           indicator is clear, and on one where it is set, leaves errno
           ERANGE.
note       Added by POSIX.1-2008 TC1 (Austin Group defect 401).
test       t/002-errno-kept.c
